WEBVTT

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:04.110
Please have whatever you want.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.800
I can vouch for the flavor.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.230
I won't be skipping the meal this time.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:10.490
It's like I'm getting healthier just by looking.

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:13.960
It's my treat, so choose whatever you like.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.440
I'll have the yellowtail daikon, water greens dressed with dried baby sardine, and a brown rice.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.060
I'll have the grilled fish and steamed vegetables.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.120
Of course.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.180
Eating that will probably thin the blood.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.130
So, what's the story today?

00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:31.580
It seems like you've escaped the slump you've been in.

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:32.630
Thanks to you.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:35.920
First of all, thank you very much.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:36.840
Don't worry about it.

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:41.320
Even without me, I think you would've eventually done the same thing.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:41.890
Besides...

00:00:42.170 --> 00:00:43.200
Besides?

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:50.910
You may not have realized it, but wasn't the reason you turned down your spot something so unexpectedly simple?

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:52.290
What's that supposed to mean?

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.400
What, indeed.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:57.910
The truth is, I have a favor to ask.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:00:59.280
What could it be?

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.300
Please teach me 5255B.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:07.040
The back two-and-a-half somersault with a two-and-a-half twist pike?

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:09.540
You say pretty funny things.

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.590
I'm being serious.

00:01:11.590 --> 00:01:17.030
No matter what, I want to take back my spot as
a representative at next month's Olympic trials.

00:01:18.650 --> 00:01:24.310
I will perfect the 5255B,
otherwise known as the Super Shrimp Special 2-0-2-0,

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:26.310
and go to the Tokyo Olympics!

00:01:26.710 --> 00:01:31.580
Is it really necessary to come up with a brand new name for a technique that already had one?

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:34.570
"SS Special 2-0-2-0" for short.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:38.320
The new name is so that I can make the move my own.

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.830
"SS Special 2-0-2-0"...

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:43.700
Sounds good. I'll help you out.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.850
I really appreciate it.

00:01:45.670 --> 00:01:47.350
Thanks for waiting.

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:48.780
Let's eat.

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:52.260
Oh, I see. This is really good.

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:53.070
Right?

00:01:55.270 --> 00:02:02.330
Someday I want to treat you to some spareribs dripping
with grease and beef stew with lots of demi-glace sauce.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:03.970
I'd certainly like to try that.

00:02:04.260 --> 00:02:06.590
But I guess that day isn't coming soon.

00:02:06.590 --> 00:02:07.980
Probably not.

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:09.950
Do you regret it?

00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:11.450
Regret what?

00:02:11.450 --> 00:02:18.590
Driving yourself to the very edge of your limits in this already extreme world.

00:02:21.920 --> 00:02:23.990
It's something I've decided for myself.

00:03:55.320 --> 00:03:56.750
Tighten up the pike more!

00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:58.250
Got it!

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:01.880
Even though she's just going to leave,

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:03.980
she's putting in all that effort teaching.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:16.770
Do you know about Coach Asaki?

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.520
Know what?

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:20.780
She's going back to America after the competition.

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:21.810
What?!

00:04:21.810 --> 00:04:24.280
I accidentally overheard.

00:04:24.990 --> 00:04:27.030
So you didn't know, huh?

00:04:28.810 --> 00:04:29.800
It doesn't matter.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.360
Right now, I just want to think about the competition.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.050
Ryou?

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:45.800
Tomo...

00:04:47.130 --> 00:04:48.300
Hey.

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:50.670
It's been a while.

00:04:52.970 --> 00:04:54.260
That's hilarious.

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:54.940
Huh?

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:59.440
I'd been avoiding that street for a while.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:02.710
It's just, running into you would've been awkward.

00:05:03.370 --> 00:05:05.950
But I was thinking it might be all right by now.

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:08.450
To think we'd meet as soon as I went that way.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.450
Like we're bound by the red thread of fate, or something?

00:05:12.260 --> 00:05:13.420
Quit it!

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:20.150
You're playing basketball now?

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:21.370
Yep.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:23.910
At the gym right by MDC.

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:24.990
Is it fun?

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:26.220
I'd say so.

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:30.060
It doesn't look like you're having much fun, though.

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:32.580
I guess not.

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:34.060
I heard from Reiji.

00:05:34.060 --> 00:05:36.240
About that lady coach.

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:37.980
He says she's going to America.

00:05:39.070 --> 00:05:40.980
Yeah, that's how it looks.

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:44.370
And that's got you discouraged, huh?

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.310
I wouldn't say discouraged...

00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:48.240
Just think it's selfish of her.

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:49.390
You're right.

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:55.000
She suddenly shows up, pushes us around like all hell, and then disappears.

00:05:56.010 --> 00:05:58.500
You know, it might be a little late,

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:03.000
but I think I'm glad to have met Coach Asaki.

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:05.870
If I had kept diving at MDC like that,

00:06:05.870 --> 00:06:09.510
I'm sure nothing would've changed,
and I never would've started playing basketball.

00:06:10.080 --> 00:06:11.610
It's the same for you too, right?

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:16.020
If the coach wasn't there, there's no way you would've been able to aim for the Olympics.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:21.170
I met with Youichi a little while ago.

00:06:21.170 --> 00:06:23.020
I asked him about this then,

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:24.920
but I wonder if you remember, Tomo.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:27.950
The Junior Olympics that we all entered.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:28.530
Huh?

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:33.260
I was really hyped, ready to appear in my new red swimsuit.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:36.040
But right before the meet, I lost the swimsuit.

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:40.040
So Youichi lent you his spare, right?

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:43.110
Yep, the really plain, gray ones.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:44.300
That's right.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:47.800
The one who hid my swimsuit back then was Youichi.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:48.800
What?!

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:52.340
It's because they stood out more than his yellow ones.

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:57.550
Even after all this time, hearing that makes me think,
"Damn it, that Youichi!"

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:00.350
So go beat him for me.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:03.560
You're the only one who can beat Youichi, right?

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:11.200
I always thought that I'd never
be able to compete with Youichi.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:16.200
But at some point I started wanting to beat him.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:17.070
Tomo.

00:07:18.570 --> 00:07:21.060
You're the one doing the diving and winning, right?

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:22.460
Not Coach Asaki.

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:25.260
You're right.

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:30.450
Get him back for my swimsuit. I'm counting on you.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:31.390
Yeah.

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:32.250
Later.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:39.600
A view that no one else has seen...

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.980
That's what I'll see!

00:07:43.570 --> 00:07:45.640
So good!

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:48.330
But I guess you're not eating any, huh?

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:48.990
That's right.

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:52.360
They're so good you'll regret it later.

00:07:52.690 --> 00:07:56.290
I mean, how can you guys be stuffing yourselves before the meet like that?

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:58.120
You really are a pain.

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:00.050
It'd be a waste not to!

00:08:00.050 --> 00:08:05.000
Coach Asaki went through the trouble of gifting us with a free half-day in Kobe.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.800
Yet the one who suggested it isn't here.

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:10.010
Has she already lost interest in us?

00:08:11.290 --> 00:08:13.010
There's no way that's true, right?

00:08:15.040 --> 00:08:16.530
It's almost time.

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:18.150
Coach Ooshima!

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:20.520
If it's MDC you're worried about, it'll be fine.

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:24.520
One of us will definitely win tomorrow's trial.

00:08:25.130 --> 00:08:30.030
We'll win by getting over 430 points and protect MDC ourselves!

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:32.610
Well, that's reassuring.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:36.420
What's wrong?

00:08:36.420 --> 00:08:38.730
Your protégé is getting this fired up.

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:41.290
Could it be that you're worried about your resig—

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:44.290
Well, the winner is going to be me anyway.

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:46.490
Big talk from a guy who can't eat a meat bun.

00:08:46.490 --> 00:08:48.670
It's not that I can't, it's that I won't.

00:08:48.670 --> 00:08:50.160
Is that a fact?

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.830
Think about the calories.

00:08:51.830 --> 00:08:53.680
You guys are as thick as thieves, huh?

00:08:53.680 --> 00:08:54.460
Right?

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:55.180
Be quiet!

00:08:54.460 --> 00:08:55.180
Stop it!

00:08:59.020 --> 00:09:00.680
Where were you guys?

00:09:00.970 --> 00:09:05.690
Just when I thought I'd finally reached Osaka with Reiji,
everyone is off touring Kobe.

00:09:06.210 --> 00:09:09.660
We were just complaining how unfair that was.

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:17.320
But Coach Fujitani took pity on us and treated us to an expensive dinner at a nice restaurant.

00:09:17.780 --> 00:09:21.300
Wouldn't you prefer that over a meat bun with an old guy?

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:22.330
Well, sorry!

00:09:23.210 --> 00:09:26.330
All right, everyone,
let's prepare for tomorrow and get rested up.

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:27.330
Yes, sir!

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:29.840
Oh yeah, Youichi.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:33.340
Coach Fujitani said to come to his room when you got back.

00:09:33.340 --> 00:09:36.850
Even when I got hurt! Even when I was chosen!

00:09:36.850 --> 00:09:40.350
You care more about MDC than me!

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:41.680
Sure.

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.440
All right, you're dismissed!

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:45.080
Wait a second!

00:09:46.870 --> 00:09:48.170
Ta-da!

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:51.360
I'll be cheering hard for everyone tomorrow.

00:09:51.650 --> 00:09:56.860
No matter who wins or who loses, I'll be cheering you on till the end!

00:09:58.430 --> 00:10:01.050
Wait, what'll we do if we burn out?

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:28.890
Do you know why I chose this place?

00:10:29.210 --> 00:10:30.400
Why did you?

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:33.870
The reason I chose this beach in Chiba as a training spot

00:10:33.870 --> 00:10:38.400
is because I wanted you to go back and stand where diving all started for you.

00:10:39.680 --> 00:10:41.870
Those are some pretty words.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:44.410
In the end, you're just going to return to America, right?

00:10:45.060 --> 00:10:48.910
I'll make you regret making me care.

00:10:52.890 --> 00:10:56.860
<i>There's a view there that no one but you can see.</i>

00:10:57.830 --> 00:10:59.660
<i>In order to see that...</i>

00:11:00.810 --> 00:11:02.440
<i>Use your eyes.</i>

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:03.900
<i>Your diamond eyes.</i>

00:11:10.340 --> 00:11:16.070
<i>If I win, I'm sure Coach Asaki will want to stay at MDC.</i>

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:17.430
<i>I'll win.</i>

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:19.550
<i>I'm going to beat Youichi and Okitsu!</i>

00:11:23.380 --> 00:11:26.080
It was a sunny day, perfect weather for an outing.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:27.080
What?

00:11:27.530 --> 00:11:29.580
How was Kobe?

00:11:30.180 --> 00:11:31.280
Oh.

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:32.780
Were you able to relax?

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:34.720
I guess.

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:37.340
Um...

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.530
What did you want to talk about?

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:41.140
Oh, sorry.

00:11:41.140 --> 00:11:43.520
Could you teach me how to use this?

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:48.660
You can take a picture by just pressing the button.

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:51.100
If you do this, you can check the pictures you took.

00:11:51.100 --> 00:11:54.750
This is to save it, and this is to delete it.

00:11:54.750 --> 00:11:56.360
I see. Thank you.

00:11:57.470 --> 00:11:58.200
Um...

00:11:58.200 --> 00:11:59.740
Hm? What is it?

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:05.740
If MDC gets shut down after tomorrow's qualifiers,
what will you do?

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:10.250
Actually, I've received an invitation from a university in Otaru.

00:12:10.660 --> 00:12:13.410
Otaru? Will you be a diving instructor?

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:15.690
No, I'll be lecturing on international sports.

00:12:16.690 --> 00:12:22.260
If MDC is shut down due to my lack of ability,
there are ways that I'll have to take responsibility for it.

00:12:23.560 --> 00:12:25.010
What is that supposed to mean?

00:12:25.970 --> 00:12:28.530
Old soldiers never die; they just fade away.

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:30.020
That's all it is.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:33.020
You can't mean you're going to
stop being a diving coach, right?

00:12:34.280 --> 00:12:35.270
There's no way.

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.770
You can't quit diving. There's just no—

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:41.230
Either way, my method of instruction is outdated.

00:12:41.230 --> 00:12:42.780
You must've noticed too.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:46.870
Is that all you wanted to say to me?

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:48.540
Oh, yes.

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:50.540
Sorry, I know it's the night before the meet.

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:51.250
It's fine.

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:05.180
Ryou?

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:21.190
Youichi, are you going somewhere?

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:24.080
Just to Tsuutenkaku.

00:13:24.080 --> 00:13:26.200
I thought I'd go get a commemorative stamp.

00:13:28.700 --> 00:13:31.210
<i>That's a lie. It's definitely training.</i>

00:13:31.700 --> 00:13:33.550
<i>Will he be all right?</i>

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:36.460
<i>Wait, what am I doing worrying about others?</i>

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:06.260
<i>If come tomorrow there isn't anyone from MDC who can win with over 430 points,</i>

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:08.910
<i>then the club will be shut down.</i>

00:14:09.600 --> 00:14:12.670
<i>The Mizuki Chairman's dying wish will go unfulfilled.</i>

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:20.500
<i>Also, it'd be like stealing everything away from
the person who poured his whole life into diving</i>

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:22.320
<i>from morning to night without a day's rest.</i>

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:26.160
<i>How could I have done this?</i>

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:27.140
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:14:36.090 --> 00:14:37.430
Fujitani Youichi.

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:39.190
Yo.

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:44.840
Hold up, Fujitani Youichi.

00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:46.690
You actually gave up your Olympic—

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:47.690
Don't say it.

00:14:48.350 --> 00:14:52.150
I've always thought you were a huge idiot,
but the reality is even worse.

00:14:52.150 --> 00:14:54.020
Yeah, I'm a huge idiot.

00:14:54.020 --> 00:14:56.950
That's what everyone from MDC just told me too.

00:14:57.330 --> 00:14:59.900
You actually responded honestly.

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:02.460
Anyway, I'm going to win tomorrow.

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:04.490
You're like a broken record.

00:15:04.490 --> 00:15:06.670
I swear I'll start hearing those words in my sleep.

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:08.190
Now it's different.

00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:08.470
Huh?

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:12.100
I want to win against you, even if it's just once.

00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:13.810
I've dived with that in mind up until now.

00:15:14.810 --> 00:15:16.350
But tomorrow will be different.

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:19.350
My battle with you is important too, of course,

00:15:20.430 --> 00:15:22.480
but I'm diving to get to the Olympics!

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:25.230
Fat chance! I'll be the one going!

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:42.500
<i>That was so stupid of me.</i>

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:46.050
<i>That wasn't the time for practice.</i>

00:15:46.050 --> 00:15:49.260
<i>I should've been preserving my stamina for tomorrow.</i>

00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:52.340
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:01.140
It's finally time.

00:16:01.140 --> 00:16:02.770
This is where we'll jump from?

00:16:03.130 --> 00:16:03.960
Yeah.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:06.770
Beyond there is the path to the Olympics.

00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:08.780
That's right.

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:17.290
Hey, Okitsu.

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:17.860
Huh?

00:16:17.860 --> 00:16:19.880
Look. They're plain.

00:16:19.880 --> 00:16:24.040
Did he realize that the battle isn't decided by the color of your swimsuit?

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:27.040
I guess we can't call him "Pinky" anymore, huh?

00:16:27.600 --> 00:16:30.240
Starting today, he's "Camel Yamada."

00:16:30.240 --> 00:16:31.260
He sure is.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:37.800
Yo. The one going to the Olympics will be me.

00:16:38.160 --> 00:16:39.810
No, it'll be me!

00:16:40.890 --> 00:16:41.810
Very well, then.

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:48.820
Youichi! Yamada's swimsuit—

00:16:56.360 --> 00:16:57.100
Hey.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:00.480
I'll be competing with big moves today too.

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:02.580
I'm going all-out with my style of diving.

00:17:03.320 --> 00:17:04.080
What about you?

00:17:04.650 --> 00:17:05.830
What are you fighting?

00:17:05.830 --> 00:17:07.160
Me?

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:08.840
Well, I guess I'd say...

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:10.840
I'm fighting myself.

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:13.120
Hey, you're pretty intense!

00:17:13.120 --> 00:17:15.390
Are you sure you don't mean insane?

00:17:15.390 --> 00:17:16.090
Huh?

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:20.910
It's fine to compete against yourself,
but in a meet, there's no point if you don't win.

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:25.850
Sorry, but I'm going to win with my thoroughly polished standard dive.

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:27.660
That's freaking underhanded!

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:29.250
I'll take that as a compliment.

00:17:29.250 --> 00:17:31.330
Are you dumb? That wasn't a compliment!

00:17:34.860 --> 00:17:36.860
All right, this should do.

00:17:37.310 --> 00:17:39.870
Right... Coach Fujitani.

00:17:40.480 --> 00:17:43.370
Do you remember what you told me before?

00:17:43.670 --> 00:17:45.650
Did I say something to you?

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:46.530
Yes.

00:17:46.530 --> 00:17:49.380
Diving is a sport that demands a great amount of time.

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:51.700
Their future is a long one.

00:17:51.700 --> 00:17:56.380
Our role is not about shortcuts,
but to teach them about the long road ahead.

00:17:57.110 --> 00:17:58.820
I said something like that?

00:17:58.820 --> 00:18:00.640
Yes, you did indeed.

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:01.970
I see.

00:18:01.970 --> 00:18:04.120
Sorry if it had you concerned.

00:18:04.120 --> 00:18:06.640
That's all right. Only recently did I understand it.

00:18:07.300 --> 00:18:14.460
The impression those words left in my heart certainly wasn't that you blindly loved MDC.

00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:18.490
I was able to meet so many superb athletes here.

00:18:18.490 --> 00:18:22.080
Those kids endured training that most adults would run from.

00:18:22.080 --> 00:18:25.160
They persevered and finally arrived here.

00:18:25.710 --> 00:18:30.170
All I can do now is confirm that with my own two eyes.

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:34.670
Yet, embarrassingly, my fingers are trembling.

00:18:36.370 --> 00:18:39.880
But I'm happy that my fingertips could tremble like this.

00:18:40.650 --> 00:18:47.180
As a coach, it's enough just to meet athletes that make you lose your judgment.

00:18:47.770 --> 00:18:50.440
Those kids have truly done well.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:54.690
Even if MDC happens to be shut down...

00:18:59.560 --> 00:19:00.980
The preliminaries have started!

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:01.700
Yeah.

00:19:01.700 --> 00:19:05.310
What are you getting nervous for, Coach Ooshima?

00:19:05.310 --> 00:19:07.950
Wait, you aren't, Sachiya?

00:19:08.250 --> 00:19:10.420
This isn't the time to be worrying.

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:14.620
Didn't I tell you? Today I'm going all-out cheering for them.

00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:21.620
Here, hold this.

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:24.220
Reiji's up next.

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:27.720
Maruyama Reiji

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:34.380
<i>He's dealing with the pressure and diving well.</i>

00:19:34.380 --> 00:19:35.730
<i>Not bad.</i>

00:19:36.730 --> 00:19:39.240
<i>The culmination of strength and beauty.</i>

00:19:42.690 --> 00:19:44.580
<i>Truly the fruits of his labor.</i>

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:47.490
<i>This is the kind of diving you should be doing.</i>

00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:50.250
<i>Your small body and your diamond eyes.</i>

00:19:50.590 --> 00:19:53.300
<i>You've made those weapons utterly yours.</i>

00:19:54.880 --> 00:19:57.340
<i>You've really improved.</i>

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:57.340
Sakai Tomoki

00:19:55.840 --> 00:19:57.340
Inward 3.5 Somersault Pike

00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:08.110
<i>His axis of rotation was out of line.</i>

00:20:08.110 --> 00:20:11.850
<i>He somehow salvaged that failed dive with a high level saving technique.</i>

00:20:12.190 --> 00:20:13.340
<i>That's not like you.</i>

00:20:14.340 --> 00:20:16.860
That wasn't like Youichi, was it?

00:20:16.860 --> 00:20:17.850
You're right.

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:19.930
He was normal up until last night.

00:20:19.930 --> 00:20:22.610
He didn't say a word at breakfast this morning, though.

00:20:22.610 --> 00:20:24.610
Back 2.5 Somersault 1.5 Twist Pike

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:28.310
Pinky is... I mean Camel is looking good.

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:30.120
Yeah, it looks like something's changed.

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:34.620
Jirou is quite the challenger, as always, but now he's seeing results.

00:20:38.500 --> 00:20:40.150
You did it, Tomo!

00:20:40.150 --> 00:20:42.130
Wow! He's in top form!

00:20:53.770 --> 00:20:54.770
Let's give it our all.

00:21:11.920 --> 00:21:12.860
Hey, Tomo.

00:21:12.860 --> 00:21:14.040
What is it?

00:21:14.350 --> 00:21:18.540
Just now, Youichi's hand was burning hot!
